2. Essential Ingredients of Section 380 IPC: Section 380 deals with an aggravated form of theft punishable with up to seven years imprisonment. To sustain a conviction under Section 380 IPC, the prosecution must establish:
(1) The commission of theft as defined under Section 378 IPC;
(2) That such theft was committed in any building, tent or vessel;
(3) That such building, tent or vessel was at the time used as a human dwelling or used for the custody of property.
